class ObjectMapper
{
    private $mappings = [];

    public function registerMapping($sourceClass, $destinationClass, $mappingFunction)
    {
        $this->mappings[$sourceClass][$destinationClass] = $mappingFunction;
    }

    public function map($sourceObject, $destinationClass)
    {
        $sourceClass = get_class($sourceObject);
        if (isset($this->mappings[$sourceClass][$destinationClass])) {
            $mappingFunction = $this->mappings[$sourceClass][$destinationClass];
            return $mappingFunction($sourceObject);
        } else {
            throw new Exception("Mapping from $sourceClass to $destinationClass is not registered.");
        }
    }
}
```

This `ObjectMapper` class allows registering mapping functions for different source and destination classes and then using those mappings to map objects from one type to another. The `map` method checks if a mapping function is registered for the given source and destination classes, and if so, it applies the mapping function to the source object to obtain the destination object. If no mapping function is registered, it throws an exception indicating that the mapping is not registered.

